            <ArticleTitle>[A double blind cross-over study with mepindolol-sulfate in patients with coronary heart disease (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>541-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">The effect of mepindolol-sulfate (2 x 2.5 mg) was tested in 20 patients with coronary heart disease in a controlled study against placebo resp. propranolol (3 x 40 mg).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">1. The frequency and intensity of anginal attacks were reduced significantly under mepindolol-sulfate therapy.-- 2. There was a significant improvement of ergometric exercise tolerance under mepindolol-sulfate therapy.--3. Additionally a reduction of ST-depression in ECG was found under mepindolol-sulfate.--4. In patients with coronary heart disease the clinical effect of mepindolol-sulfate in a daily dose of 2 x 2.5 mg was equal to propranolol in a daily dose of 3 x 40 mg.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
